<title>GERMANY: Bertelsmann picks new chairman.</title>
<headline>Bertelsmann picks new chairman.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bertelsmann AG, Europe's biggest media conglomerate, said on Friday that the man who has driven the company's push into multimedia and Internet-related services would become the group's chairman next year.</p>
<p>Thomas Middelhoff, the 44-year-old board member in charge of corporate development, will succeed Mark Woessner, who has stood at the helm of the media giant since 1983 and steps down in September 1998 after turning 60 years old.</p>
</text>
